 ## Background
-The original NeRF paper established the baseline training configuration, which has been adapted for various datasets (Blender, LLFF) and variants (Mip-NeRF, DONeRF, etc.). Subsequent works introduced specific optimizations to address issues like aliasing (Mip-NeRF), computational cost (DONeRF), defocus (AR-NeRF), and memory constraints (DP-based Selector). The field has evolved from simple MLP-based NeRFs to more complex architectures involving hash encodings (Instant-NGP, Neuralangelo) and GAN-based frameworks (StyleNeRF, AR-NeRF), each requiring tailored training configurations.
